.TH "SLIPWAY-COMPLETION" "1" "2026-09-30" "slipway 0.1.0" "Slipway Manual"
.SH NAME
slipway\-completion \- Output shell completion code for the specified shell (bash, zsh, fish)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY "slipway completion"
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I SHELL\&
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Output shell completion code for the specified shell (bash, zsh, fish).
The shell code must be evaluated to provide interactive completion of commands, resource types and names.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fISHELL\fR
The shell to output completion code for. One of: bash, zsh, fish.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
# Install bash completions where bash\-completion loads them
slipway completion bash > "${XDG_DATA_HOME:\-$HOME/.local/share}/bash\-completion/completions/slipway"
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Install zsh completions in a directory on your fpath
slipway completion zsh > ~/.zfunc/_slipway
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Install fish completions
slipway completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/slipway.fish
.EE
